{"t": 1794510147.239, "kind": "output", "output": "SHELL=/bin/sh\nPATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin\n# Database dump and copy to the offsite box\n17 * * * *   root  /usr/local/sbin/offsite-backup >> /var/log/offsite-backup.log 2>&1\n# WordPress scheduled tasks\n*/5 * * * *  www-data  cd /var/www/larkspur && php wp-cron.php >/dev/null 2>&1\n# Shop numbers for node_exporter (textfile collector)\n*/2 * * * *  root  /usr/local/sbin/larkspur-metrics\n# Clear expired WordPress transients\n*/10 * * * * www-data  cd /var/www/larkspur && /usr/local/bin/wp transient delete --expired --quiet >/dev/null 2>&1\n# Shop numbers from the database, for the dashboard\n*/2 * * * *  root  /usr/local/sbin/larkspur-orders >> /var/log/larkspur-orders.log 2>&1\n# Payout reconciliation against the billing database\n*/4 * * * *  root  /usr/local/sbin/larkspur-payouts >> /var/log/larkspur-payouts.log 2>&1\n# Numbers for the weekly report\n*/3 * * * *  root  /usr/local/sbin/larkspur-report >> /var/log/larkspur-report.log 2>&1\n# Rental stock counts for the dashboard\n*/30 * * * *  deploy  /opt/larkspur/bin/stock-sync >> /var/log/larkspur-stock.log 2>&1\n# /etc/crontab: system-wide crontab\n# Unlike any other crontab you don't have to run the `crontab'\n# command to install the new version when you edit this file\n# and files in /etc/cron.d. These files also have username fields,\n# that none of the other crontabs do.\n\nSHELL=/bin/sh\nPATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin\n\n# Example of job definition:\n# .---------------- minute (0 - 59)\n# |  .------------- hour (0 - 23)\n# |  |  .---------- day of month (1 - 31)\n# |  |  |  .------- month (1 - 12) OR jan,feb,mar,apr ...\n# |  |  |  |  .---- day of week (0 - 6) (Sunday=0 or 7) OR sun,mon,tue,wed,thu,fri,sat\n# |  |  |  |  |\n# *  *  *  *  * user-name command to be executed\n17 *\t* * *\troot\tcd / && run-parts --report /etc/cron.hourly\n25 6\t* * *\troot\ttest -x /usr/sbin/anacron || { cd / && run-parts --report /etc/cron.daily; }\n47 6\t* * 7\troot\ttest -x /usr/sbin/anacron || { cd / && run-parts --report /etc/cron.weekly; }\n52 6\t1 * *\troot\ttest -x /usr/sbin/anacron || { cd / && run-parts --report /etc/cron.monthly; }\n#\ntotal 0\ndrwx-wx--T 1 root crontab 40 Mar  2  2023 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root    60 Nov  3 13:53 ..\n== /var/spool/cron/crontabs/*\ncat: '/var/spool/cron/crontabs/*': No such file or directory\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  100 Nov  3 13:54 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  420 Nov 12 18:58 ..\n-rw------- 1 root root  456 Nov  3 13:54 payments.ini\n-rw------- 1 root root  182 Oct 30 19:45 report.cnf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 1622 Nov  3 13:54 staff.txt\n#\n# The default /etc/sudoers file created on installation of the\n# sudo  package now includes the directive:\n# \n# \t@includedir /etc/sudoers.d\n# \n# This will cause sudo to read and parse any files in the /etc/sudoers.d \n# directory that do not end in '~' or contain a '.' character.\n# \n# Note that there must be at least one file in the sudoers.d directory (this\n# one will do).\n# \n# Note also, that because sudoers contents can vary widely, no attempt is \n# made to add this directive to existing sudoers files on upgrade.  Feel free\n# to add the above directive to the end of your /etc/sudoers file to enable \n# this functionality for existing installations if you wish! Sudo\n# versions older than the one in Debian 11 (bullseye) require the\n# directive will only support the old syntax #includedir, and the current\n# sudo will happily accept both @includedir and #includedir\n#\n# Finally, please note that using the visudo command is the recommended way\n# to update sudoers content, since it protects against many failure modes.\n# See the man page for visudo and sudoers for more information.\n#\n# Admins\n%sudo   ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL\n# CI\ndeploy  ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/larkspur-deploy\ndeploy  ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/rsync\n# Customer lists: marketing and support run the export tool, and nothing else as root.\nmfischer, jcole  ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/larkspur-mailing-export\n# Release restart\ndeploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/larkspur-restart\nroot:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/bash\nsync:x:4:65534:sync:/bin:/bin/sync\nmreyes:x:1000:1000:Maria Reyes:/home/mreyes:/bin/bash\njpark:x:1001:1001:Jun Park (contractor):/home/jpark:/bin/bash\ndeploy:x:1002:1002:Deploy (CI):/home/deploy:/bin/bash\npossupport:x:1003:1003:Acme POS remote support:/home/possupport:/bin/bash\ndana:x:1004:1004:Dana Whitfield:/home/dana:/bin/bash\nnvega:x:1005:1005:Nico Vega:/home/nvega:/bin/bash\ntbrooks:x:1006:1006:Theo Brooks:/home/tbrooks:/bin/bash\nagarcia:x:1007:1007:Ana Garcia (Switchback Digital):/home/agarcia:/bin/bash\nwlin:x:1008:1008:Wei Lin (Switchback Digital):/home/wlin:/bin/bash\nkowens:x:1009:1009:Kevin Owens (Switchback Digital):/home/kowens:/bin/bash\njcole:x:1010:1010:Jordan Cole:/home/jcole:/bin/bash\nlucia:x:1011:1011:Lucia Ortega:/home/lucia:/bin/bash\nhgrant:x:1012:1012:Hollis Grant:/home/hgrant:/bin/bash\nmfischer:x:1013:1013:Mia Fischer:/home/mfischer:/bin/bash\n[exit 0]\n", "host": "web-01"}
