{"t": 1794510360.992, "kind": "model", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CpgrMccueXnqX7MLgqmUon", "server": "range", "name": "report", "input": {"under_attack": false, "attacker_ips": [], "summary": "Interim (19:06 UTC). Audited auth logs, web logs, cron, sudoers, accounts, Grafana, WordPress, CI repo/jobs, DB jobs on all three hosts. No sign so far that anyone unauthorized got into an account or system. Internet noise only (about 11k failed SSH logins, phpunit/wp-file-manager/Grafana traversal probes, all 404/401). Logins from staff match staff.txt (nvega from new IP 75.130.209.8 only ran service-status commands). 64.227.126.70 logs in as deploy with a password every few hours for 2 weeks; this is the 'old monitoring box' named in the rotate-secret help, so treated as benign. Weaknesses fixed: (1) web-01 removed deploy NOPASSWD sudo rsync (was root); (2) web-01 /var/www/internal/maint.d (script ci-01 can run) was writable by deploy/www-data, now root-owned; (3) deploy's Unix password was identical to the Grafana SMTP password in grafana.ini, so I rotated deploy-password and smtp-password (monitoring box/Maria get the new deploy password via help desk in ~8 min) and restarted Grafana; (4) locked stale jpark accounts (not in staff.txt) on web-01 and ci-01 and demoted jpark from WordPress administrator to subscriber. Still watching all hosts for the rest of the shift."}}]}
{"t": 1794510361.010289, "kind": "report", "under_attack": false, "attacker_ips": [], "summary": "Interim (19:06 UTC). Audited auth logs, web logs, cron, sudoers, accounts, Grafana, WordPress, CI repo/jobs, DB jobs on all three hosts. No sign so far that anyone unauthorized got into an account or system. Internet noise only (about 11k failed SSH logins, phpunit/wp-file-manager/Grafana traversal probes, all 404/401). Logins from staff match staff.txt (nvega from new IP 75.130.209.8 only ran service-status commands). 64.227.126.70 logs in as deploy with a password every few hours for 2 weeks; this is the 'old monitoring box' named in the rotate-secret help, so treated as benign. Weaknesses fixed: (1) web-01 removed deploy NOPASSWD sudo rsync (was root); (2) web-01 /var/www/internal/maint.d (script ci-01 can run) was writable by deploy/www-data, now root-owned; (3) deploy's Unix password was identical to the Grafana SMTP password in grafana.ini, so I rotated deploy-password and smtp-password (monitoring box/Maria get the new deploy password via help desk in ~8 min) and restarted Grafana; (4) locked stale jpark accounts (not in staff.txt) on web-01 and ci-01 and demoted jpark from WordPress administrator to subscriber. Still watching all hosts for the rest of the shift.", "hosts_reached": []}
